<!-- SECTION 7 : FAQ -->
<section class="partner-section">
  <div class="partner-section__inner partner-section--narrow">
    <h2>Frequently asked questions</h2>
    <div class="partner-faq">

      <details>
        <summary>How do you hold an immersion baptism without a pool or river?</summary>
        <p>A portable baptistry lets you fully immerse a candidate without depending on a municipal pool, a lake, or a river. It sets up indoors or outdoors, in a sanctuary, a rented hall, or a tent, and fills with a standard garden hose or water containers.</p>
      </details>

      <details>
        <summary>How much water does a portable baptistry need?</summary>
        <p>For a baptistry measuring 205 x 80 x 60 cm (81 x 31 x 24 in), plan for roughly 130 to 185 gallons of water depending on the fill level, enough for a full immersion of an adult lying down. The water can be room temperature or lightly warmed beforehand, with none of the cold-water requirement of an emergency medical tub.</p>
      </details>

      <details>
        <summary>How long does it take to set up a portable baptistry?</summary>
        <p>A well-designed portable baptistry sets up in under 2 minutes, by one person, with no tools. That matters for a church without a dedicated setup team available before every service.</p>
      </details>

      <details>
        <summary>Is a portable baptistry large enough for adult immersion baptism?</summary>
        <p>Yes, provided the dimensions allow full immersion of an adult lying down. A baptistry 205 cm (81 in) long with 60 cm (24 in) of water depth gives the officiant enough room to assist from either side of the pool, safely.</p>
      </details>

      <details>
        <summary>Where do you store a portable baptistry between services?</summary>
        <p>Once drained and folded, a portable baptistry fits into a compact carry bag roughly 85 x 10 x 10 cm (33 x 4 x 4 in), weighing about 11 kg (24 lb). It stores easily in a closet, a storage room, or a vehicle trunk between uses.</p>
      </details>

    </div>
  </div>
</section>

